   "bucket": "reasoning",
   "planned_path": "P5",
   "scion_answer": "To find the $2007^{\\text{th}}$ digit to the right of the decimal point in $\\frac{1}{7}$, we first determine the decimal expansion of $\\frac{1}{7}$:\n\n$$\\frac{1}{7} = 0.142857142857...$$\n\nThe decimal expansion has a repeating cycle of length 6: $142857$.\n\nTo find the $2007^{\\text{th}}$ digit, we compute $2007 \\mod 6$:\n\n$$2007 = 334 \\times 6 + 3$$\n\nSo $2007 \\mod 6 = 3$.\n\nThis means the $2007^{\\text{th}}$ digit corresponds to the $3^{\\text{rd}}$ digit in the repeating cycle $142857$, which is $2$.\n\nTherefore, the $2007^{\\text{th}}$ digit to the right of the decimal point in $\\frac{1}{7}$ is $\\boxed{2}$.",
