   "id": "math-0020",
   "bucket": "reasoning",
   "planned_path": "P5",
   "scion_answer": "To round $6287215$ to the nearest ten thousand, we look at the digit in the ten thousands place and the digit in the thousands place (which determines whether we round up or down).\n\nThe number $6287215$ can be written as:\n$$6287215 = 6 \\times 10^6 + 2 \\times 10^5 + 8 \\times 10^4 + 7 \\times 10^3 + 2 \\times 10^2 + 1 \\times 10^1 + 5 \\times 10^0$$\n\n- The **ten thousands** place has the digit **8**.\n- The **thousands** place has the digit **7**.\n\nSince the thousands digit is $7 \\geq 5$, we **round up**.\n\nSo we increase the ten thousands digit from $8$ to $9$, and replace all lower digits with zeros:\n\n$$6287215 \\approx 6290000$$\n\n**Verification:**\n- The ten thousand below: $6280000$\n- The ten thousand above: $6290000$\n- Midpoint: $6285000$\n- Since $6287215 > 6285000$, we round up to $6290000$.\n\n$$\\boxed{6290000}$$",
